lens:
Luxury art direction for jewellery e-commerce (Mejuri / Missoma / Monica Vinader calibre) with Indian fine-jewellery taste, round 6: elegance, typography, photography sequence and crops, spacing and grid, colour, hierarchy, copy tone, and whether a Rs 2,399 piece feels worth desiring.

G3 passes. fold.png, added.png, fold-ad.png, screens_1-5.jpg and measure.json (06:59:17-21) are newer than prototype.html (06:58:55, md5 74dcaeee...). My renders of an untouched copy (same md5) agree: H1 399-427, facts end 562, bar 575, no console errors. fold.png is md5-identical to round 5's (d4ae18d6...), so the 360x640 first screen did not change. fold-ad.png is byte-identical to fold.png, by the builder's choice.

I found no G1 trip from this lens. A grep of the page text, alt text, aria labels, JSON-LD, title and meta description finds only allowed text: 'Returns are for manufacturing faults only', 'PVD 18K gold coating', 'No reviews for this piece yet', 'Refunds are considered case by case' and the FAQ's 'Is it real silver? No.'

All seven of my round-5 fixes landed in some form:
- the inert ticks are text;
- slide 5 has one plate;
- tall screens get the 3:4 frame;
- the set caption names the bag;
- text-wrap: pretty is applied;
- the footer ends on a clean edge;
- 'nosug' is gone. It went CRO's way, as a 'slim' card instead of my two-line form; see C20.

Two round-5 changes made things worse from this lens:
1. The bag's new foot policy line grew the foot to 154px. In a two-piece bag at 360x640 the Total figure (459-496) is now sliced by the foot's hairline at 486. In round 3 it sat whole above a foot at 511.
2. The slim card names no piece. The ring's photo and name sit directly under 'Added to your bag · 1 piece' and read as the piece just added. Every 320x568 shopper gets it on a first add from the top.

Also found:
- at 320 the suggestion row (card and bag) breaks inside the ring's name and its rupee line;
- Up close still repeats slide 2, with its top third in bokeh.

